      "tags": [],
      "description": "Make `scene` the one [`ctx.scene`](/docs/api/three-context) / [`ctx.camera`](/docs/api/three-context)\npoint at, and the one the renderer draws. Same scene is a no-op. A scene that was\nnever passed to [`addScene`](/docs/api/three-start) throws.\n\nComponents on the previous scene receive `onDisable` and pause; components on the\nnew scene resume (`onEnable`) or, the first time after `start()`, run the full\nbootstrap. [`ContextModule`](/docs/api/context-module)s keep running."
    },
    {
      "name": "start",
      "params": [],
      "returns": "this",
      "returnsHtml": "<span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">this</span>",
      "signature": "() => this",
      "signatureHtml": "<span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">() </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> this</span>",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Bootstrap the active scene: awaken registered [`ContextModule`](/docs/api/context-module)s, attach\nthe context to the scene graph, and activate [`Object3DBehaviour`](/docs/api/object3d-behaviour)\ninstances on every existing object. After `start()`, any objects added to the active scene get\nbootstrapped automatically. Other registered scenes wait until the first [`setScene`](/docs/api/three-start)\nthat shows them.\n\nNo more modules can be registered after this call."
    },
